---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro"
import { UPDATE_DISCLOSURE, GITHUB_URL } from "../lib/copy"
// QUO-325: Noam approved the complete Terms page on 2026-10-24.
// Operator name supplied by Noam: QuotaCanary; no company status is asserted.
// Israeli governing law approved; published 2026-10-29 on Noam's go.
// This draft does not assert completed service shutdown.
---

<Layout title="Terms of use - QuotaCanary" description="Terms for the free, local Mac app and self-host source." path="/terms">
  <article class="page page-narrow wrap">
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="eyebrow page-meta">Last updated 29 October 2026.</p>
    <p class="page-meta">Operator: QuotaCanary.</p>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>QuotaCanary is free, open-source software for checking API credit balances. Use only credentials you are authorized to use and follow each vendor’s terms.</p>
<h2>Checks and alerts</h2>
<p>Checks and alerts require the app to be running and your Mac awake and online. Vendor changes, network failures, permissions and software errors can interrupt them. Keep another way to check critical balances.</p>
<h2>Keys and updates</h2>
<p>Vendor keys stay in the Mac’s login Keychain and go directly to their vendors, never to QuotaCanary servers.</p>
<p>{UPDATE_DISCLOSURE}</p>
<h2>Source and self-hosting</h2>
<p>The source is provided under the <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/blob/main/LICENSE`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">MIT license</a>, including its warranty disclaimer. If you run the web version yourself, you operate its server, database, credentials and polling schedule.</p>
<h2>Stopping use</h2>
<p>You can stop using the app at any time. Use Erase local data to remove its stored credentials and files before uninstalling if you want those removed.</p>
<h2>Governing law</h2>
<p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Israel.</p>
<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Questions: <a href="mailto:hey@quotacanary.com">hey@quotacanary.com</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
